id: pm-sbqn4h
title: "MCP pm_comments lists only the newest 20 comments by default: the backward output cursor stops at that producer page and the last page reports has_more without a continuation"
description: "Found 2026-11-08 by the CodeRabbit review of PR 1685. A pm_comments MCP listing without limit or full is bounded by the producer to the newest 20 comments (runMcpCommentsAction sets limit 20 and includeMeta), with total_count and has_more true when more exist. A universal output cursor pages only within that producer page. On an item with more than 20 comments, following next_cursor backwards under a small outputBudget therefore stops after the 20th-newest comment. The last page still reports has_more true (from the producer) but carries no next_cursor, so an agent cannot tell how to reach older comments except by restarting with options.limit or options.full true, which the tool description mentions. Expected: when the producer page is exhausted, the envelope names the producer continuation, for example a cursor or a suggested limit for the next older window, so has_more true never arrives without an executable continuation. Duplicate check: searched MCP comments default 20 has_more continuation producer page. pm-gh1679 (open) owns a producer cursor for item history, which is the analogous design, and pm-8s53lj (closed) made the output cursor page backwards within the producer page."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[5]: agent-ux,annotations,continuation,mcp,read-output
created_at: "2026-11-08T03:54:47.662Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-08T14:41:06.003Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-08T13:44:58.261Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-08T13:44:58.261Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "An MCP comments listing whose producer page is exhausted names a continuation to the next older window, or reports has_more only when a continuation is present; A spec drives tools/call on more than 20 comments and reaches the oldest comment by following continuations alone"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
repro_steps: "Through MCP tools/call, list pm_comments on an item with more than 20 comments with a small outputBudget and follow next_cursor until it disappears, then read has_more"
resolution: "runMcpCommentsAction no longer sets an implicit limit of 20. A listing sets includeMeta for total_count and has_more and leaves the bound to the default output budget, whose ordered_suffix retention keeps the newest comments and issues a backward cursor, exactly like pm_notes, pm_learnings and the CLI. options.limit=N still selects the newest N. The pm_comments tool description, the contract snapshot and docs/READ_OUTPUT_CONTRACTS.md record the change."
expected_result: "Following next_cursor alone reaches the oldest comment, and has_more is true only while a continuation is present"
actual_result: "On 30 comments of about 310 characters, tools/call returned indexes 12-30 with has_more true and next_cursor, then 1-11 with has_more false and no cursor; the spec asserts has_more equals the presence of a cursor on every page"
